  "definitions": {
    "accuracy": "JNLI choice and JCommonsenseQA: the first largest probability is the label, a permuted row maps its answer back to the original option; JNLI noul: P(true) > 0.5 is true and P(true) = 0.5 is false",
    "auroc": "P(true) of the JNLI noul rows ranked with entailment as the positive class, ties count one half, undefined with one class",
    "brier_hard": "mean of (P(true) - y)^2 with y = 1 for entailment and 0 for contradiction and neutral",
    "difference": "stage 3 minus stage 1' on the same rows, wrapper and temperature: quantization and execution path together",
    "jsts": "E[p] = sum k p(k) against the continuous label: MAE, Pearson and Spearman (average ranks for ties), undefined when either side is constant",
    "permutations": "stage 3, adopted JCommonsenseQA variant: the options in the four fixed orders, the label position follows its option, and the answers are mapped back to the original options",
    "scope": "Descriptive results on 200 rows per task without a pass line and without intervals; they are not a claim of Japanese quality or of calibration",
    "temperatures": "1 and the adopted temperatures of the calibrated bundle (decision.json per_kind); probabilities are recomputed from the 24 logits of each stage"
